{"type":"message","timestamp":"2026-06-11T12:09:23.964Z","role":"user","content":"You are a Gemini worker on the Rust browser engine `underrated`. Work ONLY inside this worktree (cwd). Commit your work before finishing. All code, comments, and the commit message MUST be in English.\n\nCONTEXT — review feedback on task t0268 (ul bullet markers):\nThe previous commit on this branch changed the ul list marker in `src/layout/mod.rs` to emit Unicode bullet code points per `list-style-type`:\n  - disc   -> U+2022 (•)\n  - circle -> U+25E6 (◦)\n  - square -> U+25AA (▪)\nThat layout change is CORRECT and must stay. BUT the bitmap font in `src/font/mod.rs` only has glyphs for ASCII 0x20-0x7E; every other code point falls back to the `.notdef` box. So all three markers currently render as identical TOFU boxes (□) in the shipping render path — a visual regression from the previously-visible '*'. A headless PNG confirmed the tofu.\n\nYOUR TASK (single module: `src/font/mod.rs` only):\nAdd real 8x8 glyphs for the three bullet code points so they render instead of `.notdef`. Keep the ASCII path and `.notdef` fallback unchanged.\n\nImplementation guidance:\n- The glyph table is `const BITMAPS: [u64; 96]` (indices 0..=94 = chars 0x20..=0x7E, index 95 = .notdef), expanded by `expand_bitmaps`. `glyph_coverage(c)` and `glyph_width(c)` map chars to indices.\n- Extend the table to 99 entries: append three new bitmaps at indices 96, 97, 98 for U+2022, U+25E6, U+25AA respectively. Update the `[u64; 96]` / `96 * 8 * 8` sizes accordingly (96 -> 99) wherever they appear, and the `.notdef` index stays 95.\n- In `glyph_coverage` and `glyph_width`, add a match for these three code points BEFORE the `.notdef` fallback, returning index 96/97/98. Keep glyph width = the fixed monospace advance (same as other glyphs).\n- Suggested bitmaps (row 0 = top byte, bit 7 = leftmost pixel), tune if you like but they must look like a filled disc / hollow circle / filled square:\n    U+2022 • filled disc : 0x00183C7E7E3C1800\n    U+25E6 ◦ hollow circle: 0x0018244242241800\n    U+25AA ▪ filled square : 0x00003C3C3C3C0000\n\nTESTS (add to the `#[cfg(test)]` module in `src/font/mod.rs`):\n- A test asserting `glyph_coverage('\\u{2022}')`, `'\\u{25E6}'`, `'\\u{25AA}'` each return a NON-empty slice that is DIFFERENT from `glyph_coverage('\\u{FFFF}')` (the .notdef box), and that each has at least one non-zero coverage byte.\n- A test asserting the three bullets produce three DISTINCT coverage slices from each other (so the styles are visually distinguishable).\n\nVERIFY before committing:\n- `cargo test` (all green), `cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings` (clean), `cargo fmt --check` (clean).\n- Do NOT touch any file other than `src/font/mod.rs`. Do NOT skip/ignore/delete existing tests.\n- No `unwrap()`/`expect()` in non-test code.\n\nThen commit on the current branch:\n  git add -A && git commit -m \"fix(font): add disc/circle/square bullet glyphs so ul markers render (t0268)\""}
